    "scan_cost_multiple_same_corpus": 2.33,
    "mechanism": "The hash embedder produces a handful of near-identical motif vectors, so cluster-boundary queries barely split their neighbours and nprobe=6 held the tail. Real 768d all-mpnet embeddings are continuous and spread across the sphere, so a boundary query's true neighbours genuinely straddle two centroids: at nprobe=1, 4 of 90 boundary queries return NOTHING (min 0.000) and the boundary class means 0.730. The first probe count whose p1 recall@10 clears 0.8 on real geometry is 14, and holding that tail costs a 25.5% scan fraction vs the 10.9% nprobe=6 bought on the same corpus \u2014 2.3x the scan. That scan cost is the latency the recall contract is paid for; it is the number S16 stands on. The hash value flattered the engine because its geometry had no real boundaries to fail on."
  },
